# Security Rules

## Authentication

- Never roll custom auth — use the established auth library for this project
- JWTs must have an expiry (`exp` claim)
- Refresh tokens must be rotated on use
- Failed login attempts must be rate-limited

## Authorization

- Check permissions at the service layer, not just the route layer
- Never trust client-supplied user IDs — derive identity from the session/token
- Principle of least privilege: request only the permissions actually needed

## Data handling

- Never log PII (emails, names, IDs in combination, payment info)
- Sanitize all user input before using in queries (parameterized queries only)
- Never interpolate user input into SQL strings
- Encrypt sensitive fields at rest (PII, tokens, secrets)

## Secrets

- Secrets go in environment variables only — never hardcoded
- Never commit `.env` files
- Rotate any secret that was accidentally logged or exposed

## External requests

- Validate webhooks with signatures (e.g., Stripe-Signature header)
- Set timeouts on all outgoing HTTP requests
- Never forward raw external payloads to internal systems without validation
